  <title>Print product label</title>

  <p>Open it with <gui>Print label</gui> in the menu of <link
  xref="products"/> or in the <link xref="product_hub"/>.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Printer</gui>: a Zebra label printer, or
    <gui>System</gui> to print a LibreOffice label template on an ordinary
    printer.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the label <gui>Template</gui>.</p></item>
    <item><p>Choose the <gui>Product</gui>, or scan or type its
    <gui>Barcode</gui> and press <key>Enter</key>. Choose the
    <gui>Location</gui>; the product's shelf location there is filled in, and
    can be changed for this label.</p></item>
    <item><p>Click <gui>Print label</gui>, or press
    <keyseq><key>Ctrl</key><key>P</key></keyseq>.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <p>To print many labels quickly, check <gui>Print label</gui> beside the
  barcode: a label then prints each time a product is chosen or a barcode is
  found. For a system template, <gui>View label</gui> opens it in LibreOffice
  instead of printing. <gui>Edit</gui> opens a Zebra template in the <link
  xref="zebra_designer"/>; it asks for the administrator password.</p>

</page>
